      "subtype": "missing_trace_family",
      "summary": "An s-witness family is a (d+1)-uniform family in which each member has an s-subset absent from its intersection trace; W_{d,s}(n) denotes its maximum possible cardinality.",
      "title": "s-witness family and extremal function",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-21T19:39:07Z"
